+  <h1>Story 7.1 — round 4: top-down, our designs, Blender-built</h1>
+  <div class="answer">
+    <b>Your r3 verdict:</b> <q>still not happy with the design of the nodes, they look amaturish. Mini motorway was sinple and still elegant. design something in blender please. I wuld like them in top down look like mini motorway. also can you design some houses in blender?</q>
+    <p style="margin-top:8px"><b>Done:</b> true top-down (the Mini Motorways view — a steep tilt where you read the <b>roof</b>, not the facade), simple + elegant, and every shape is ours — designed and rendered in Blender (the family is also sitting in your live Blender scene, saved as <code>_probe/blender/packet-plumber-buildings-td.blend</code>). No MM assets, no purchased assets, flat emissive only, pixels land on the exact look-book hexes.</p>
+    <p style="margin-top:6px"><b>Your depth note (the Blender 3/4 screenshot):</b> added — buildings carry depth two ways, both painted-flat (no gradients): the <b>walls are one darker tone</b> (the shaded-side read from your screenshot) and each node casts a <b>soft flat contact shadow</b> down-right (drawn by the game as a translucent ink ellipse — Blender's hashed alpha dithers at sprite size, so the shadow lives in the renderer). <b>Zoomed lanes:</b> the r4 note ("hard to see the 3 queues") — the three lane stripes now separate with wider canvas gutters at zoom; riders sit centered in their lane.</p>
+  </div>
+
+  <div class="verdict">
+    <b>Settled so far (your rounds 1–3):</b> pipes = <b>tier-colored band + inset motorway lane stripes</b>; whisper grid; bigger ringed packets; the 5.5 popover chrome idiom; <b>focus-zoom camera</b> (click a node/link → smooth eased zoom in, lanes + queues reveal on zoom-in, back out when done — alerts-as-nav zooms to the problem); bridges parked as an era-6 (SDN) candidate.
+  </div>
+
+  <h2><span class="tag new">the redesign</span> The top-down family (Blender sprites → the game draws them)</h2>
+  <div class="card">
+    <p class="sub">The sprite set, rendered in Blender (flat emissive, canon hexes): 4 residential houses (canon body/roof pairs) · the content host (flat roof + the YouTune play-marking + antenna) · the data center (cooling grid) · router pucks (basic / mid / high — the canon round hubs).</p>
+    <img class="sheet" src="sheet-td.png" alt="top-down sprite family">
+    <ul class="notes">
+      <li><b>House:</b> the two-tone gable roof IS the read (roof complement colors) + a chimney nub + a shaded wall tone + a soft contact shadow. Simple, elegant, never a bare rectangle.</li>
+      <li><b>Content host:</b> flat roof + the big play-button roof marking (the destination roof-sign, MM's idiom translated) + rooftop vent + antenna.</li>
+      <li><b>Data center:</b> long flat roof + cooling-unit grid.</li>
+      <li><b>Pucks:</b> the concentric hub — rim, face, core, LED ring(s) — tier-scaled, smooth circles.</li>
+    </ul>
+  </div>
+
+  <div class="card">
+    <p class="sub" style="margin-top:2px"><b>In-game, the live busy frame</b> (the game's own renderer drawing those sprites; merged pipes; doorstep queues; telegraph + chrome):</p>
+    <img class="frame" src="variant-1-d1-village.png" alt="top-down buildings in the live frame">
+  </div>
+
+  <h2>Camera stills (your focus-zoom direction)</h2>
+  <div class="card grid2">
+    <figure><img class="frame" src="variant-1-d1-village.png" alt="bird's-eye"><figcaption><b>Bird's-eye:</b> calm tier bands; lanes stay a hint. Queued packets pile at the doorstep — roofs stay clean.</figcaption></figure>
+    <figure><img class="frame" src="zoom-bundle.png" alt="zoomed"><figcaption><b>Zoomed (clicked):</b> the full lane read — the express-heavy 4:2:1 split on the wide trunk, a streaming triangle riding its lane, the puck's LED ring.</figcaption></figure>
+  </div>
+
+  <h2>Notes</h2>
